{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility","id":1493720,"title":"W20 and Revised book compatibility","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-26T07:29:37-07:00","id":1493720,"title":"W20 and Revised book compatibility","content":"My group has decided to start or dive into the World of Darkness, from Pathfinder 2. After researching our options, we have decided to go with W20. I have done a lot of searching on the internet for guidance, but would really appreciate some assistance with the following.<br /> <br /> 1. We have decided as a group that required reading before session 0 would be the character generation rules in the core book, the revised tribe book matching the tribe the character will be, the relevant section of the Book of Auspices. Does this seem like a good list? Any suggestions or amendments?<br /> <br /> 2. I was thinking about picking up Players Guide to Garou as well (revised player guide). How relevant is this to W20?<br /> <br /> 3. I have figured the majority of the setting information is applicable between Revised and W20. How about mechanics? I read somewhere that there is a a very high degree of compatibility. Is this accurate? Any pitfalls I should be watching out for?<br /> <br /> Thanks so much for the assistance and I look forward to participating in the forums.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter","name":"Awesomeotter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T07:58:59-07:00","id":1493725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Awesomeotter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility#post1493720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group has decided to start or dive into the World of Darkness, from Pathfinder 2. After researching our options, we have decided to go with W20. I have done a lot of searching on the internet for guidance, but would really appreciate some assistance with the following.<br /> <br /> 1. We have decided as a group that required reading before session 0 would be the character generation rules in the core book, the revised tribe book matching the tribe the character will be, the relevant section of the Book of Auspices. Does this seem like a good list? Any suggestions or amendments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just skip CoG Revised, in that case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. I was thinking about picking up Players Guide to Garou as well (revised player guide). How relevant is this to W20? </div> </div> </div>There are a few Gifts that didn't make it into W20, so it should still have some utility. Revised has an issue with Pure Breed lining up with human ethnic groups, though, so disregard that where you run into them in the Revised source. Also, some of the Gifts from Revised were, well, revised for W20. I'd use the W20 version where applicable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. I have figured the majority of the setting information is applicable between Revised and W20. How about mechanics? I read somewhere that there is a a very high degree of compatibility. Is this accurate? Any pitfalls I should be watching out for? </div> </div> </div>W20 is mostly timeline neutral. Revised has some metaplot changes - the Get of Fenris killing off the Swords of Heimdall, Margrave Konietzko uniting the Garou of Europe, and the destruction of the Seventh Generation cult, most prominently. You'll probably find out more if you use the Revised-era tribebooks. These aren't really pitfalls, though, so much as module-like features to use, since W:tA was always very metaplot-light, especially in comparison to the fare of &quot;watch the starring official characters anticlimactically resolve a situation like the worst deus ex machina&quot; that you see extensively in Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks so much for the assistance and I look forward to participating in the forums. </div> </div> </div>Hopefully, our discussion and speculation of W5 hasn't risen to concerning levels. (^VVVV^)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T08:12:18-07:00","id":1493727,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick reply. I had read on here that the CoG revised book was really bad. Luckily, it seems like everyone has decided to make Glasswalker characters so that shouldn't be an issue.<br /> <br /> I have read the discussions on here regarding W5, and honestly they helped a lot. We decided we were not keen on the direction the new W5 was taking and it really cemented our choice to go full throttle into W20/revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter","name":"Awesomeotter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T10:07:23-07:00","id":1493741,"title":"","content":"Glass Walkers revised is brilliant. So an excellent choice if you want to flesh out the tribe more. I pretty much agree with everything Dino said, but I'm curious if you're not concerned about that being a LOT of stuff to read to play? Are they ok with having to read around 200-400 pages just to play?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T10:19:24-07:00","id":1493743,"title":"","content":"Hi Asmodai! Our main concern is that our prior gaming experience has been too much &quot;Roll play&quot; and not enough &quot;Role play&quot;. When we discussed it as a group, there seemed to be a general consensus that in order to actually successfully role play in a new setting, everyone had to have a decent understanding of the world. I do think that some of the players were less thrilled about the idea that there would be mandatory reading, and will inevitably do more skimming then actual reading. We will be taking a month off of gaming to give everyone time to at least attempt to get familiar with the setting. We will then circle back and have a session 0 where we will make characters together and come up with a concept for the story. I agree that the reading is a bit daunting and it is a concern. If a player is unable to finish it or has trouble absorbing the information, I hope that the session 0 will help bring everyone onto the same page. The biggest concern I have is that as the storyteller, I don't have any practical experience with the setting either, so I am counting on onboarding into W20 being a collaborative process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter","name":"Awesomeotter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T11:25:32-07:00","id":1493750,"title":"","content":"There is an out-of-character account of the life of a Kinfolk in, I think, Players Guide to the Garou or Storytellers Handbook revised. It is only one paragraph, but it is the only out of character account I know of (I haven't read W20 Kinfolk completely).<br /> <br /> You might run a game, where Kinfolk doesn't play a large part, and then you might not run into discrepancies when different players have different baselines on what behaviour towards Kinfolk is common or acceptable for garou in general (adjustments due to tribal or local culture not withstanding).<br /> <br /> But if you tend towards a recurring supporting cast of NPCs you might want to establish which views the PCs and NPCs have on the matter. I found, that for many readers, and the in-character texts in supplements, the mistreatment of Kinfolk is very present in the books, because it is mentioned often in passing. This leads to the (mis)conception, that garou are per definition bullies or even serial-rapists. &quot;Kinfolk: Unsing Heroes&quot; is more nuanced, but even here some people seem to only remember the horrible experiences of the NPCs described in the &quot;Kinfolk of Note&quot; Appendinx and see them as a baseline - despite the accounts of the Kinfolk-narrators in the other chapters of the books.<br /> <br /> So, reading this out-of-character paragraph, if you can find it, and discuss with the players how you as a group see the Garou/Kinfolk-relationship might be a good idea.<br /> <br /> In addition to that, W20 makes a point (and enforces them with some changes in game mechanics) that Kinfolk of any age could in theory have a First Change. This, in my opinion, also changes the Garou/Kinfolk-dynamic and might be something to keep in mind when reading the revised material. Back in revised, garou were in general rather certain, if a person was garou or not (since a Gift allowed to check with relative ease and garou offspring would be a reason for celebration, so asking a pack/sept mate to use the Gift on one's extended family would make sense). Also, having the First Change later in life was something rather unusual in earlier editions, while W20 makes it seem a bit more common (although still not the norm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 09-26-2022, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T13:14:12-07:00","id":1493761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Awesomeotter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility?p=1493743#post1493743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Asmodai! Our main concern is that our prior gaming experience has been too much &quot;Roll play&quot; and not enough &quot;Role play&quot;. When we discussed it as a group, there seemed to be a general consensus that in order to actually successfully role play in a new setting, everyone had to have a decent understanding of the world. I do think that some of the players were less thrilled about the idea that there would be mandatory reading, and will inevitably do more skimming then actual reading. We will be taking a month off of gaming to give everyone time to at least attempt to get familiar with the setting. We will then circle back and have a session 0 where we will make characters together and come up with a concept for the story. I agree that the reading is a bit daunting and it is a concern. If a player is unable to finish it or has trouble absorbing the information, I hope that the session 0 will help bring everyone onto the same page. The biggest concern I have is that as the storyteller, I don't have any practical experience with the setting either, so I am counting on onboarding into W20 being a collaborative process.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool and sounds fun. I'm just so used to being the one that teaches others that don't have the time/inclination for deep dives that it's cool to see a group approaching it like this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T06:49:26-07:00","id":1493900,"title":"","content":"One of our players has decided he would like to play Lupus and was thinking about getting the Ways of the Wolf book. I took a quick look at it and it looks like it was a 1st edition sourcebook. Is there anything that is still relevant to W20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter","name":"Awesomeotter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T06:57:34-07:00","id":1493901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Awesomeotter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility?p=1493900#post1493900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of our players has decided he would like to play Lupus and was thinking about getting the Ways of the Wolf book. I took a quick look at it and it looks like it was a 1st edition sourcebook. Is there anything that is still relevant to W20?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd skip it. It's not the best of the books, and you'd learn more from Red Talons revised than from that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T08:08:38-07:00","id":1493902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility?p=1493901#post1493901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd skip it. It's not the best of the books, and you'd learn more from Red Talons revised than from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally speaking, I wouldn't go with either. RT Revised was written by Matt McFarland, and there are Red Talon perspectives that aren't shared by all lupus, especially not lupus Glass Walkers. For now, it's best to keep in mind that lupus are going to have issues with being Garou due to not being able to really have a family the way that wolves do, and also because they're surrounded by humans who have deeply entrenched and very incorrect ideas about how wolves work. That and getting wrong-footed because of the sense shift from wolf to human (have to rely on only audiovisual instead of olfactory and hearing), in general keeping in mind the living space of a wolf, are the key things to keep in mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T22:49:41-07:00","id":1493952,"title":"","content":"I'll double down on the worries presented previously by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> that this is too much. This <b>is too much to start</b>.<br /> <br /> W20 was made in such a way to have everything you need to play, and believe me, it has everything you need to play. Most X20 books are really, really good at including almost everything relevant made previously and making it easy to swallow, and W20 isn't an exception. There are hiccups, bot overall you'll be ok just with that.<br /> <br /> Trying to take in too much after a long time playing only one other game will just overload you all with information you won't be able to apply any time soon. And it won't solve your perceived problem, actually it has more chances of worsening it, as with more rules to know and want to apply, you're more likely to pay too much attention to them.<br /> <br /> Seriously, take a step down and focus on what matters. Read the core, and focus on the parts of the core required for your game. When you have some experience and fun, then you go deeper. And don't worry about the players not knowing everything about the tribe, most of the time it is expected that the PCs be newbies themselves with a lot of gaps in their knowledge of Garou society, as it is a society of creatures that grow up mostly out of it even when they know about it, so the core is also as much or even more than most new Cliath will know anyways.<br /> <br /> After this time, then by all means, a Revised Tribebook will probably help, and the Players Guide may do so, too. But they also have both a lot of material already in the W20 core and some ditched with good reason, so you won't take as much out of them, but they'll definitely help with lore and mood.<br /> <br /> Nothing will help with wolf-born. Well, maybe watching something on Discovery Channel, that'll be better than anything officially released ever in the setting on this matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T13:02:04-07:00","id":1493991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility?p=1493901#post1493901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd skip it. It's not the best of the books, and you'd learn more from Red Talons revised than from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like Ways of the Wolf. But it is definitely not a &quot;Players Guide to Lupus.&quot; Instead, it includes various things to help players and ST run a wilderness chronicle. Lupus are a big part of it. But there are major parts of the book that go into various monsters that can be found in the wilderness, examples of the Great Beasts, a list of plants that can be awakened and turned into talens, a primer on wolves (some of which has been dated badly, but others still relevant) and wilderness survival. Plus the usual pages of new Gifts, Rites, Fetishes, etc.<br /> <br /> Probably only 20 of its 70 pages directly address the lupus (most of which can probably be figured out on your own especially if you have other sourcebooks), but the rest would be relevant in some way.<br /> <br /> As an ST I find it very useful and one of my key sourcebooks. But it may not be worth it for a player who just wants to play a lupus per <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27612_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27612\" data-vbnamecard=\"27612\">Awesomeotter</a> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T13:07:44-07:00","id":1493993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility?p=1493991#post1493991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually like Ways of the Wolf. But it is definitely not a &quot;Players Guide to Lupus.&quot; Instead, it includes various things to help players and ST run a wilderness chronicle. Lupus are a big part of it. But there are major parts of the book that go into various monsters that can be found in the wilderness, examples of the Great Beasts, a list of plants that can be awakened and turned into talens, a primer on wolves (some of which has been dated badly, but others still relevant) and wilderness survival. Plus the usual pages of new Gifts, Rites, Fetishes, etc.<br /> <br /> Probably only 20 of its 70 pages directly address the lupus (most of which can probably be figured out on your own especially if you have other sourcebooks), but the rest would be relevant in some way.<br /> <br /> As an ST I find it very useful and one of my key sourcebooks. But it may not be worth it for a player who just wants to play a lupus per <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27612_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27612\" data-vbnamecard=\"27612\">Awesomeotter</a> .</div> </div> </div> </div>The Great Beasts do kind of suffer from an early installment mechanical shrug of god, though - while WoD games are still rather mechanically shaky, non-avian dinosaurs and 60 plus foot long sharks with a Strength of only 10-15 is some BS (and the problem persists in the huge forms of Mokole).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T06:13:35-07:00","id":1495970,"title":"","content":"Hello! I just wanted to thank everyone again for their insight. We did complete our session 0 and everything went well. I picked up a bunch of splat books and for the most part the players are really enjoying reading them. We decided as a group to ease up on the requirement of reading, as one player just was not getting on board and I did not want to alienate him. Everyone seems to be enjoying their own little Werewolf niche. One player is gobbling up Hammer and Klaive and another Book of the City. Combined together, we will be Werewolf pros. ;-)<br /> <br /> New question, in your opinion want makes a better add-in to a Werewolf game. Mummy 2nd edition or Mummy the Resurrection. Either as allies or antagonists. The game will be taking place in Chicago for the most part and will center around a pack of Glasswalkers. I am aware of Under a Blood Red Moon supplement and I did purchase/read it. This is not the version of Chicago we are going with though. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27612-awesomeotter","name":"Awesomeotter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T15:59:59-07:00","id":1496010,"title":"","content":"The original Mummy tries to emulate the original Universal Studios monster movies of the Mummy (or its spin offs like Anne Rice's Mummy: Ramses the Damned). So if you want to play something similar to Boris Karloff in the Mummy, that is the book you use. (The later Mummy movies with less intelligent mummies murdering people are more like the Bane Mummies of the book intended as antagonists).<br /> <br /> I really don't know what Mummy the Resurrection is trying to do. Its characters don't match my ideas of a mummy at all. So I think the game is garbage, but some people like it.<br /> <br /> I think either kind would work in a Werewolf game. It just depends on how you want to use it.<br /> <br /> But I think a better approach is to decide what kind of mummy you want, and then pick whichever sourcebook best emulates that. Obviously I would choose the original Mummy, but everyone has different tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T17:43:51-07:00","id":1496014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Awesomeotter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1493720-w20-and-revised-book-compatibility?p=1495970#post1495970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! I just wanted to thank everyone again for their insight. We did complete our session 0 and everything went well. I picked up a bunch of splat books and for the most part the players are really enjoying reading them. We decided as a group to ease up on the requirement of reading, as one player just was not getting on board and I did not want to alienate him. Everyone seems to be enjoying their own little Werewolf niche. One player is gobbling up Hammer and Klaive and another Book of the City. Combined together, we will be Werewolf pros. ;-)<br /> <br /> New question, in your opinion want makes a better add-in to a Werewolf game. Mummy 2nd edition or Mummy the Resurrection. Either as allies or antagonists. The game will be taking place in Chicago for the most part and will center around a pack of Glasswalkers. I am aware of Under a Blood Red Moon supplement and I did purchase/read it. This is not the version of Chicago we are going with though. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy 2 is going to give you more mileage. Mostly because the new Mummies of Resurrection are deeply tied to North Africa and the Middle East, and don't work as well outside of that region, plust the focus of the book is all over. Mummy 2 still has the Shemsu Heru that will have reasons to work with Garou here and there even if they may not agree on everything, and the Bane Mummies are there as evil sorceror mummies that you might want. There's also a number of other mummies listed in the book, including native american mummies you could build for the game without the Egyptian trappings.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}